Contributors|H. S. P. M&uuml;ller
comments|Details of the fit have been published in<br><font color="#064898">
comments|(1) H. S. P. M&uuml;ller and S. Br&uuml;nken,
comments|2005, <i>J. Mol. Spectrosc.</i>, <b>232</b>, 213</font>.<br>
comments|A considerable number of rotational transitions was taken from that
comments|work. Additional <i>v</i><sub>2</sub> = 0, 1 transition frequencies
comments|were taken from the compilation of<br><font color="#064898">
comments|(2) F. J. Lovas 1985, <i>J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data</i>
comments|<b>14</b>, 395</font>; from<br><font color="#064898">
comments|(3) S. C. Mehrotra, G. Bestmann, H. Dreizler, and H. M&auml;der,
comments|1984, <i>Z. Naturforsch.</i> <b>39a</b>, 633</font>; from<br><font color="#064898">
comments|(4) S. C. Mehrotra, H. Dreizler, and H. M&auml;der,
comments|1984, <i>Z. Naturforsch.</i> <b>40a</b>, 683</font>; from<br><font color="#064898">
comments|(5) P. A. Helminger and F. C. De Lucia
comments|1985, <i>J. Mol. Spectrosc.</i> <b>111</b>, 66</font>; from<br><font color="#064898">
comments|(6) E. A. Alekseev, S. F. Dyubko, V. V. Ilyushin, and S. V. Podnos
comments|1996, <i>J. Mol. Spectrosc.</i> <b>176</b>, 316;</font> and from<br><font color="#064898">
comments|(7) H. S. P. M&uuml;ller, J. Farhoomand, E. A. Cohen,
comments|B. Brupbacher-Gatehouse, M. Sch&auml;fer, A. Bauder, and G. Winnewisser,
comments|2000, <i>J. Mol. Spectrosc.</i>, <b>201</b>, 1</font>.<br>
comments|Further <i>v</i> = 0 data were taken from<br><font color="#064898">
comments|(8) S. P. Belov, M. Y. Tretyakov, I. N. Kozin, E. Klisch,
comments|G. Winnewisser, W. J. Lafferty, and J.-M. Flaud,
comments|1998, <i>J. Mol. Spectrosc.</i> <b>191</b>, 17</font>.<br>
comments|The <i>v</i><sub>2</sub> = 1 &#150; 0 energy difference was
comments|determined by including &nu;<sub>2</sub> infrared transitions
comments|from<br><font color="#064898">
comments|J.-M. Flaud, A. Perrin, L. M. Salah, and W. J. Lafferty,
comments|1993, <i>J. Mol. Spectrosc.</i> <b>160</b>, 272</font>.<br>
comments|Transitions with uncertainties much larger than those at
comments|similar frequencies and with similar quantum numbers have not
comments|been merged.<br>
comments|The precision of the predicted uncertainties of the
comments|transition frequencies should be reliable up to about
comments|3<i>K"<sub>a</sub></i> + <i>J"</i> &asymp; 100.
comments|The calibration uncertainty has been estimated in (3)
comments|to be 0.0003&nbsp;cm<sup>&#150;1</sup>.<br>
comments|The transition dipole moment has been derived from<br><font color="#064898">
comments|(10) B. Sumpf,
comments|1999, <i>Spectrochim. Acta</i> <b>A 55</b>, 1931</font>.<br>
comments|The uncertainty in the transition dipole moment is about
comments|8&nbsp;%. <font color="#FF0050"><b>NOTE:</b></font> default
comments|intensities are given for 300&nbsp;K&nbsp;!
comments|The partition function includes both vibrational states.
comments|The individual contributions (> 0) are given in parentheses.<br>
